<title>USA: Shell restarts Alabama facility.</title>
<headline>Shell restarts Alabama facility.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil Co restarted its 74,000 barrel-a-day chemical plant Sunday in Saraland, Alabama, after shutting it down Friday ahead of the arrival of Hurricane Danny.</p>
<p>&quot;We're now operating at full capacity,&quot; said Noel Wheeler, external affairs manager. The plant suffered no damage as a result of the storm, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We never lost power so it worked out pretty well,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The facility produces mostly chemical feedstocks for Shell's Deer Park, Texas and Norco, Louisiana refineries.</p>
<p>((--Matt Daily, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620))</p>
